{"tool_name":"bracken","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"bracken","version":"3.1p1","home":"https://github.com/jenniferlu717/Bracken","documentation":"https://github.com/jenniferlu717/Bracken/blob/v3.1p1/README.md","license":"GPL-3.0-or-later","summary":"Bracken (Bayesian Reestimation of Abundance with KrakEN) is a highly accurate statistical method that computes the abundance of species in DNA sequences from a metagenomics sample.","identifiers":["biotools:Bracken","usegalaxy-eu:est_abundance","doi:10.7717/peerj-cs.104"],"license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"number":0,"run_exports":[null],"skip":true},"requirements":{"build":[null,null,"make"],"host":["llvm-openmp","libgomp"],"run":["python","kraken2"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/jenniferlu717/Bracken/archive/v3.1.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["bracken -h","bracken-build -h","est_abundance.py -h","generate_kmer_distribution.py -h","kmer2read_distr --help","combine_bracken_outputs.py -h"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"bracken","identifiers":["biotools:Bracken","doi:10.7717/peerj-cs.104"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Bracken (Bayesian Reestimation of Abundance with KrakEN) is a highly accurate statistical method that computes the abundance of species in DNA sequences from a metagenomics sample.","home_url":"https://github.com/jenniferlu717/Bracken","keywords":["Metagenomics","Microbial ecology","Genomics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":3292},"biotools":{"id":"bracken","home":"https://ccb.jhu.edu/software/bracken/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Bracken is a companion program to Kraken 1, KrakenUniq, or Kraken 2 While Kraken classifies reads to multiple levels in the taxonomic tree, Bracken allows estimation of abundance at a single level using those classifications (e.g. Bracken can estimate abundance of species within a sample).","addition_date":"2017-08-20T15:17:20Z","last_update_date":"2025-06-11T12:25:29.118910Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:bracken","credit":[{"email":"jlu26@jhmi.edu","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://ccb.jhu.edu/software/bracken/index.shtml?t=manual"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-CZ","animalandcropgenomics","bebatut","vashokan"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Statistical calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2238"}]}],"name":"Bracken","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.7717/peerj-cs.104","metadata":{"abstract":"Metagenomic experiments attempt to characterize microbial communities using high-throughput DNA sequencing. Identification of the microorganisms in a sample provides information about the genetic profile, population structure, and role of microorganisms within an environment. Until recently, most metagenomics studies focused on high-level characterization at the level of phyla, or alternatively sequenced the 16S ribosomalRNAgene that is present in bacterial species. As the cost of sequencing has fallen, though, metagenomics experiments have increasingly used unbiased shotgun sequencing to capture all the organisms in a sample. This approach requires a method for estimating abundance directly from the raw read data. Here we describe a fast, accurate new method that computes the abundance at the species level using the reads collected in a metagenomics experiment. Bracken (Bayesian Reestimation of Abundance after Classification with KrakEN) uses the taxonomic assignments made by Kraken, a very fast read-level classifier, along with information about the genomes themselves to estimate abundance at the species level, the genus level, or above. We demonstrate that Bracken can produce accurate species- and genus-level abundance estimates even when a sample contains multiple near-identical species.","authors":[{"name":"Breitwieser F.P."},{"name":"Lu J."},{"name":"Salzberg S.L."},{"name":"Thielen P."}],"citationCount":1084,"date":"2017-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PeerJ Computer Science","title":"Bracken: Estimating species abundance in metagenomics data"},"type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Metagenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3174"},{"term":"Microbial ecology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3697"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Bracken","home":"https://bio.tools/bracken","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Bracken is a companion program to Kraken 1, KrakenUniq, or Kraken 2 While Kraken classifies reads to multiple levels in the taxonomic tree, Bracken allows estimation of abundance at a single level using those classifications (e.g. Bracken can estimate abundance of species within a sample).","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"3.1","first_commit":"2019-10-15","conda_name":"bracken","conda_version":"3.1p1","summary":"Bayesian Reestimation of Abundance with KrakEN","edam_operations":["Statistical calculation"],"edam_topics":["Metagenomics","Microbial ecology"],"toolshed_categories":["Sequence Analysis","Metagenomics"],"toolshed_id":"bracken","users_5_years":2842,"users_all_time":2842,"usage_5_years":157181,"usage_all_time":157181,"bio_tools_summary":"Bracken is a companion program to Kraken 1, KrakenUniq, or Kraken 2 While Kraken classifies reads to multiple levels in the taxonomic tree, Bracken allows estimation of abundance at a single level using those classifications (e.g. Bracken can estimate abundance of species within a sample).","bio_tools_ids":"bracken","bio_tools_name":"Bracken","related_tutorials":["https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/ecology/tutorials/bacterial-isolate-species-contamination-checking/tutorial.html","https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/microbiome/tutorials/taxonomic-profiling/tutorial.html","https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/sequence-analysis/tutorials